(a) Any animal at-large or otherwise in violation of the provisions of this chapter may be impounded in the animal shelter or a designated location in a humane manner. The animal must be claimed by the owner or his representative within three days.
(b) The following animals may be impounded, but are not limited solely to:
(1) Animals running at-large;
(2) Animals, the ownership of which is unknown;
(3) Vicious dogs;
(4) Female dogs/cats in heat and off the premises of their owners;
(5) Dogs/cats which have bitten a person or animal or which had been bitten by a dog or animal suspected of having rabies;
(6) Dogs/cats not vaccinated for rabies within the preceding 12 months;
(7) Dogs/cats which have strayed from the premises of their owners;
(8) Dogs/cats suspected of having rabies;
(9) Unconfined dogs/cats in quarantine areas.
(c) If an animal so impounded has not been reclaimed by its owner or his representative within three days in accordance with the provisions of this chapter, such animal shall become the absolute property of the animal control unit, which may convey ownership of such animal to any responsible person on such conditions as the animal control unit may prescribe or the animal control unit may humanely destroy such animal.
